# QoS-2 flow with optional interleaved events.
#
# Between PUBLISH and PUBREL the client may send:
#   - additional PUBLISH messages (same msgid, DUP=1 or new id) -- triggers CVE-2023-28366 style patterns
#   - PINGREQ keepalives
# After PUBREL the client may send PINGREQ keepalives only.
#
# Total session bounded to 30 s.  Inner Kleene-star gaps bounded to 10 s each.
# Client events only: CONNECT, PUBLISH, PUBREL, PINGREQ, DISCONNECT.
# Broker responses (CONNACK, PUBREC, PUBCOMP, PINGRESP) are checked in the harness.
#
# n >= 4 (mandatory: CONNECT, PUBLISH, PUBREL, DISCONNECT)
# n = 5  -> one extra event between PUBLISH and PUBREL (PUBLISH or PINGREQ)
# n >= 6 -> multiple extras possible

<CONNECT.PUBLISH.<(PUBLISH+PINGREQ)*>_[0,10].PUBREL.<PINGREQ*>_[0,10].DISCONNECT>_[0,30]
